opam-version: "2.0"
name: "rocq-pi-leibniz"
version: "1.0.5"
synopsis:
  "Constructive pi for the Rocq constructive Cauchy reals — premise-free separation from every rational with extractable witnesses"
description: """
A constructive pi for the constructive Cauchy reals of the Rocq standard
library ([ConstructiveCauchyReals]), realized by the alternating Leibniz
series, with the strong irrationality separation theorem

  Theorem pi_leibniz_strong_irrational_prop :
    forall a b : Q, b <> 0 -> CReal_appart pi_leibniz (inject_Q (a / b)).

together with its premise-free companion

  Theorem pi_leibniz_appart_all_Q :
    forall q : Q, CReal_appart pi_leibniz (inject_Q q).

v1.0.5 adds two significant contributions:

  - Sqrt2UniformStrongIrrational: Bishop's uniform constructive lower
    bound 1/(3b²) for √2, carried by a sigT Set-level witness with four
    witness-value assertions; extraction audit clean on both faces.

  - PiMu0Cos: the μ₀-cos window-family modulus piece, providing pointwise
    separation-window search for 22/7 and 355/113 with a transparent
    decider (mu0cos_sep_dec) and smoke assertions.

pi is apart, in the sense of [CReal_appart], from every embedded rational
constant; the apartness witness comes with an explicit positive margin and
an explicit convergence modulus for the realizer.  Every witness is
explicitly constructed and the statements are [Set]-valued throughout.
Both main statements are premise-free and closed under the global context.
The content modules compile green on Rocq 9.3.0.
"""
